# Session log discipline (`docs/SESSIONS.md`)

Cursor-side mirror of the Claude Code `warn-session-log` stop hook
(`.claude/hookify.session-log.local.md`). This repo runs from several concurrent
Cursor **and** Claude Code worktrees with no chronological timeline otherwise, so a
missed entry makes a session unresumable and hides parallel-session collisions.

> **Incident this closes:** the 2026-07-12 four-firms prop-portfolio ADR
> (`docs/adr/2026-07-12-prop-portfolio-four-friendly-firms.md`, recorded by a Cursor
> Cloud Agent) landed on `main` with **no** SESSIONS entry — there was no Cursor-side
> session-log rule at the time.

## When to write

At **session wrap-up**, if the session shipped code, recorded a decision
(ADR / notice / brief), or moved live-ops state → append a reverse-chronological entry
(**newest on top**) to `docs/SESSIONS.md`.

**SKIP** trivial / read-only turns (a question answered, a file read, a one-line fix).
Do not add noise.

## Entry shape (append-only; link out, never restate canonical values)

- **Focus** — what the session set out to do
- **Shipped** — branch + commit + concrete deltas (link artifacts, don't duplicate)
- **Decisions/defects** — link the ADR / notice / brief produced
- **Open / next** — lead line is `STATE queue: #1 <title> · #2 <title> · #3 <title>`
  (titles + owner links). Do not copy leftover names from the previous top entry.
  Residue after the lead only with `queue-exception: <reason>` and an existing owner.
- **Live-ops state** — lock / allocation / gate status where relevant

Canonical owner: `docs/operational_rules.md §7`. Do **not** restate risk %, MC anchor,
strategy versions, or hashes — link to their owners (`CLAUDE.md`, `docs/adr/`, `LOCK.md`).
User rules override this file.
